# HOD Digital Signature & Approval Workflow

Implement a complete HOD workflow: signature upload during onboarding, one-click approval with automatic digital signature + cryptographic hologram, server-side PDF generation, and approved PDF download on the applicant dashboard.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **PDF Generation Strategy:** The plan uses **Puppeteer** (headless Chrome) for server-side PDF generation because your existing frontend `pdfGenerator.ts` already uses an HTML template approach (`html2pdf.js`). Puppeteer will reuse the same HTML/CSS template on the backend, producing pixel-perfect A4 PDFs with embedded signatures and hologram. This avoids re-implementing the entire template with a low-level library like `pdfkit`.

> [!WARNING]
> **Breaking Change — Prisma Migration:** This adds new columns to `User` and `Application` models. You'll need to run `npx prisma migrate dev` after schema changes. Existing data won't be affected (all new fields are optional).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **HOD Onboarding:** HODs are created by CC Admin (existing `/users/register` or admin endpoint). This plan does NOT add a self-registration flow for HODs — they must be onboarded by an admin who assigns them `role: HOD` and a `departmentId`.

