### 2. Backend — HOD Signature Upload

#### [MODIFY] [users.controller.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/backend/src/modules/users/users.controller.ts)

Add two new endpoints:

- **`POST /api/v1/users/me/signature`** — HOD uploads their signature image
  - Protected by `JwtAuthGuard` + `RolesGuard` (HOD only)
  - Uses `FileInterceptor` with `diskStorage` to save to `./uploads/signatures/`
  - Validates file type (JPEG/PNG only), max 1MB
  - Saves the file path to `user.signatureStoragePath`

- **`GET /api/v1/users/me/signature`** — Check if HOD has uploaded a signature
  - Returns `{ hasSignature: true/false }` so the frontend can gate the Approve button

#### [MODIFY] [users.service.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/backend/src/modules/users/users.service.ts)

Add methods:
- `uploadSignature(userId: string, filePath: string)` — Updates `signatureStoragePath` on the User record
- `getSignatureStatus(userId: string)` — Returns whether a signature exists
- `getSignaturePath(userId: string)` — Returns the actual file path (internal use by PDF service)

